Johnstown Pennsylvania one of the  overlooked bygone cities that made  Donald Trump president the mines and  mills that once filled these valleys  with smoke and jobs haven't been  resurrected as he promised things were  hardly thriving here before coronavirus  but life in lockdown has brought this  city to a complete standstill giving  people plenty of time to observe how the  man they elected is handling the crisis  that will define his presidency so you  feel Donald Trump's briefings have been  informative yes very much so living  alone during lockdown gale is feeling  fatigue she misses her church she misses  company she's been watching the man she  voted for closely have you ever worried  throughout all of this that Donald Trump  is putting his own political interest in  terms of the economy over people's  health no no not at all because I think  for the most part he has been listening  to his elfin health experts on his on  his team but it's a dual edged sword  you know if the economy is ruined we're  going to suffer that decades from now  and people will die just as if they had  the virus because poverty does kill  people what went through your mind when  he floated the idea of injecting  disinfectant and he did that  tongue-in-cheek at did he i I believe so  yes indeed the tone seemed pretty  serious sometimes he does that I mean  I've been at at least one rally of his  and okay even if it was a joke is it the  time for jokes well I think if you took  everybody's comments and wrote them down  there are times that maybe in an  inappropriate comment he's not everybody  he's the president in a global pandemic  that's true well I took it as a joke I  was flabbergasted  I actually just was like really know  he's yeah he is serious he's actually  serious he's going with this Tammy also  voted for Trump in 2016 but for her  Corona  virus is the last straw she says his  daily briefings have offered her no  reassurance they are in my opinion a  platform for him to feed his ego that  he's in charge that he can be rude to  people and he can also put everyone else  down and how they've done everything  wrong and he's done everything right and  nothing is his fault and he takes no  accountability for anything but Tammy  says she senses that her change of heart  isn't the prevailing sentiment for  plenty of people Trump is still the  savior his impatience to reopen the  economy is deeply felt in places like  Johnstown where unemployment was already  70 percent above the national average  but the polls say most people support  ongoing restrictions keeping families  safe is the priority rushing things  could be catastrophic for Americans and  for the man who's leading them Amanda  Walker Sky News Johnstown Pennsylvania
 

